Toko sat next to me, across from Ms. Hasegawa.\nMeanwhile, I faced Takeshi -- I actually hadn't seen him\nin a while.%K%P
都子坐在我的旁边，长谷川同学坐在她的正面。\n而同样很令人怀念的刚志君，和我正对着…%K%P
However, now that we had both suffered one or two wounds\nthrough love, we could no longer look at each other with\nresolute eyes -- instead, our gazes darted nervously from\ncorner to corner.%K%P
只是，我们彼此都是受过伤的人，\n他收起了过去那种刺人的视线，\n和我时不时互相交换着有些尴尬的视线。%K%P
This stood in complete contrast to the girls, who were\nboth looking each other in the eye.%K%P
…与彼此撇开视线的女性阵形成对照。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dH-How are you doing, Takeshi?\nHas the Soccer Club started practice yet?\d%K%P
