May was nearing its end. I spent all of Golden Week and\nthe last few weekends working my butt off to the point I\neven lost track of time, but it was definitely the latter\nhalf of May now.%K%P
５月下旬。\n最近既没有黄金周也没有周六周日，都让人失去了季节感，\n但今天毫无疑问是５月的下旬。%K%P
I'd been counting the days -- no, the hours -- until this\npayout.%K%P
也是每个月都期待着、\n这个月更是掰着指头数等着的发工资日。%K%P
...That being said, I'd completely forgotten about it just\nnow, as I was busy with the details of a new project.%K%P
…话是这么说，不过刚才忙过头了，都忘掉了。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI-I wonder how much I got...\nI need at least... um...\d%K%P
「有、有多少呢…？\n目标额是，那个…」%K%P
%LCKinoshita
%LC木下
\dYou completely ignored the limits set by the Labor\nStandards Act both this month and the last. I imagine the\nnumbers on that slip must be quite incredible.\d%K%P
「上个月和这个月都完美无视了劳动基准法呢。\n这工资额一定不小吧？」%K%P
...I hoped they were.\nOr rather, I'd be in trouble if they weren't.%K%P
…希望如此。\n不，如果不是就头疼了。%K%P
After all, I had to exceed the amount of my June salary\njust by doing overtime in April and May.%K%P
不管怎么说，我不仅仅得挣到四月和这个月的工资，\n六月的基本工资也要挣到才行…%K%P
